WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.260
- I was 12 years old.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.444
- I was 13 years old.

00:00:02.444 --> 00:00:03.767
- I was 12 years old.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.947
- I was 13 years old when I was bullied.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.220
- When I was bullied there were
confrontations in hallways.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.563
- It was pretty much directly
face to face, verbal, contact.

00:00:16.563 --> 00:00:21.277
- I was being called a name
from my so called friends.

00:00:21.277 --> 00:00:24.040
- Some person that I
don't know slammed my head

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.455
into the locker and called me a chink.

00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:28.382
And they just walked away.

00:00:28.382 --> 00:00:32.004
- I was dealing with a lot
of, you know, acne problems.

00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:33.885
This guy, he would just call me pizza face

00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:34.814
in front of people.

00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:37.623
- I was just walking through the cafeteria

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:41.617
and someone called me a faggot.

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:45.285
It was kind of like my
whole body had chills

00:00:45.285 --> 00:00:47.259
and I didn't know what to do.

00:00:47.259 --> 00:00:49.279
- They all giggled and laughed.

00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:51.740
And it actually was a word in Cantonese

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.133
and I don't speak Cantonese.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:56.314
I think now I would say like,
(speaks foreign language).

00:00:56.314 --> 00:00:59.356
What they were calling
me was little fat girl.

00:00:59.356 --> 00:01:02.142
- This kid turned around
to me with a Sharpie marker

00:01:02.142 --> 00:01:05.068
and for all the classmates
to hear and he said,

00:01:05.068 --> 00:01:07.599
"Hey Zach, bend over, I
wanna play connect the dots

00:01:07.599 --> 00:01:08.876
"with your face."

00:01:08.876 --> 00:01:10.919
- I was so embarrassed when it happened.

00:01:10.919 --> 00:01:13.752
Bullies made me feel so
bad about my ethnicity.

00:01:13.752 --> 00:01:15.609
Like, I really did internalize that.

00:01:15.609 --> 00:01:20.137
- It made me feel like I
wasn't as good as anybody else.

00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:22.505
- I didn't really know what is friendship

00:01:22.505 --> 00:01:24.827
if the people you think you're close to

00:01:24.827 --> 00:01:26.058
are laughing at you.

00:01:26.058 --> 00:01:28.728
- It was something that
was really heartbreaking

00:01:28.728 --> 00:01:30.005
for my mom to see.

00:01:30.005 --> 00:01:32.606
I remember she just always
looked so sad for me

00:01:32.606 --> 00:01:36.808
because I was just being myself.

00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:41.808
And me being myself meant
that I was being bullied.

00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:45.423
- You just have this fear, in
middle school, in high school,

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:46.769
that you're going to be called that

00:01:46.769 --> 00:01:48.859
for the rest of your life.

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:52.063
- [Voiceover] Now it's a
word that I look back on

00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:55.291
and I use it to see how far I've come.

00:01:55.291 --> 00:01:57.759
- [Zach] You know, I realized
that that's not who I am.

00:01:57.759 --> 00:01:59.500
I haven't been that since I was you know,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.172
13, 14 years old.

00:02:01.172 --> 00:02:03.308
- [Voiceover] No matter what
people think, I can accomplish

00:02:03.308 --> 00:02:04.399
anything that I want.

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:05.955
I was doing great things.

00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:08.416
I had great friends, a great family.

00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:12.038
- [Voiceover] I love my
life and I am more than just

00:02:12.038 --> 00:02:13.362
a little fat girl.

00:02:13.362 --> 00:02:14.801
- [Voiceover] That word
does not define me.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.543
It never did define me.

00:02:16.543 --> 00:02:18.075
I'm so much more as a person.

00:02:18.075 --> 00:02:20.263
- [Voiceover] I could be
whoever I wanted to be

00:02:20.263 --> 00:02:23.073
and I was extremely proud of being Asian.

00:02:23.073 --> 00:02:24.559
- [Voiceover] I am great.

00:02:24.559 --> 00:02:25.627
I am happy.

00:02:25.627 --> 00:02:28.134
I am anything that I want to be.

00:02:28.134 --> 00:02:30.294
- There's gonna be a
time where you realize

00:02:30.294 --> 00:02:32.546
that the thing that people target you for

00:02:32.546 --> 00:02:34.357
is actually your greatest asset.

00:02:34.357 --> 00:02:37.167
- I recommend building a support system

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:40.371
and help each other learn that you are

00:02:40.371 --> 00:02:42.136
more than those words.

00:02:42.136 --> 00:02:45.572
- If you be yourself, you grow
up to be who you want to be,

00:02:45.572 --> 00:02:48.219
you're gonna be a great
person, no matter what.

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:51.400
- You are so much more
than any of the words

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.020
that anyone could say to you.

